; bqmx_negative_size: a size that is not an allocation raises, rather than
; installing an empty model for free.
;
; Every allocator used to read its size through
; `usize::try_from(..).unwrap_or(0)` on Rust, so `PUSH -1 / BQMX r0` halted
; Ok with a size-0 model and a zero charge, while xqvm_py raised a bare
; ValueError outside the XQVMError hierarchy -- which the harness reports as
; "stdout did not parse as JSON" rather than as a divergence. Two
; instructions, verifier-clean, and no vector anywhere.
;
; The same `unwrap_or(0)` swallowed any size above u32::MAX on wasm32, which
; is the runtime the Substrate pallet executes in, so five billion variables
; were an empty model charged nothing inside the runtime and a real model on
; a native node. That half has no in-repo home; it is pinned by the
; crate-local `an_allocator_size_is_charged_before_it_is_narrowed`.

PUSH -1
BQMX r0
HALT
